    "markerTop": 692.15
  },
  {
    "slide": 2,
    "marker": "sh/nu58f2hs",
    "text": "sh/wjy9sry9",
    "label": "In 2025, Microsoft introduced the idea of the Agent Boss: an employee who builds, delegates to, and manages agents.",
    "markerTop": 757.15
  },
  {
    "slide": 2,
    "marker": "sh/xk7qlczu",
    "text": "sh/ahwrqhgj",
    "label": "OpenAI defines agents as systems that can complete workflows on a user’s behalf, rather than simply answer questions.",
    "markerTop": 797.15
  },
  {
    "slide": 2,
    "marker": "sh/bip8jmho",
    "text": "sh/cnupgny5",
    "label": "Google describes enterprise agents as systems that connect models with company data, tools, memory, orchestration, and runtime infrastructure.",
    "markerTop": 837.15
  },
  {
    "slide": 2,
    "marker": "sh/do3q9szq",
    "text": "sh/t8byxkn2",
    "label": "Anthropic’s research suggests that people tend to decide what should be done, while agents make more of the execution decisions about how to do it.",
    "markerTop": 877.15
  },
  {
    "slide": 4,
    "marker": "sh/0ba143al",
    "text": "sh/rm1k7yt4",
